meta {
  name: 16b. Cleanup - Delete DataStructure
  type: http
  seq: 47
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datastructures/:id
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: {{sagaDataStructureId}}
}

tests {
  test("DataStructure deleted or already gone", function() {
    const status = res.getStatus();
    // 204=deleted, 404=already gone, 409=still referenced
    expect(status === 204 || status === 404 || status === 409).to.be.true;
  });
}

docs {
  **Saga cleanup step 16b of 18** — Teardown phase: remove resources created during the saga.

  Deletes the DataStructure created in step 3b. Must run after the dataset has been deleted (step 13), since released datasets may reference this DataStructure.

  **Expected Response:** 204 No Content. 404 if already deleted. 409 if one of its versions is still referenced.

  **Post-condition:** DataStructure record removed from `portal_backend` DB.
}
